It's expensive to go out and drink.

1078
00:43:05.770 --> 00:43:08.870
Yeah, and, like, pay for the high-priced cocktails.

1079
00:43:08.990 --> 00:43:09.350
Yeah.

1080
00:43:09.690 --> 00:43:09.830
Yeah.

1081
00:43:10.190 --> 00:43:10.430
Yeah.

1082
00:43:10.730 --> 00:43:11.430
All right.

1083
00:43:11.590 --> 00:43:14.610
Number two, do you speak any other languages?

1084
00:43:15.470 --> 00:43:19.550
I have taken German and French, and I can read it pretty well.

1085
00:43:19.750 --> 00:43:20.950
I can't understand it.

1086
00:43:21.250 --> 00:43:21.630
Okay.

1087
00:43:21.630 --> 00:43:23.870
If someone's speaking it, unfortunately.

1088
00:43:24.130 --> 00:43:25.130
But you can read it.

1089
00:43:25.210 --> 00:43:25.870
I can read it.

1090
00:43:26.190 --> 00:43:27.710
Has that come in handy ever?

1091
00:43:27.970 --> 00:43:34.430
I did get to go to the Olympics this past summer, so, yeah, it came in a little bit handy,

1092
00:43:34.490 --> 00:43:38.290
but I was also, like, too nervous to trust my instincts.

1093
00:43:38.450 --> 00:43:41.490
So, luckily, you know, we had guides and everything.

1094
00:43:42.710 --> 00:43:43.190
Okay.

1095
00:43:43.190 --> 00:43:47.970
Okay, number three, what's a place you've been to that you absolutely loved?

1096
00:43:48.470 --> 00:43:54.570
I love New Orleans so much that I talked my husband into buying a condo there.

1097
00:43:54.730 --> 00:43:55.510
Oh, wow.

1098
00:43:55.530 --> 00:43:58.970
So, we have the tiniest little condo in the French Quarter.

1099
00:43:59.970 --> 00:44:01.270
I love it.

1100
00:44:01.350 --> 00:44:03.030
It's like living in the middle of Disneyland.

1101
00:44:03.530 --> 00:44:04.550
It's so fun.

1102
00:44:04.550 --> 00:44:07.490
That town just has a whole energy to it.

1103
00:44:07.490 --> 00:44:07.690
Doesn't it?

1104
00:44:07.730 --> 00:44:08.810
It's just so cool.

1105
00:44:09.090 --> 00:44:09.330
Yeah.

1106
00:44:09.410 --> 00:44:09.590
Yeah.

1107
00:44:09.730 --> 00:44:10.270
I love it.

1108
00:44:10.350 --> 00:44:12.290
And we go as often as we can.

1109
00:44:12.470 --> 00:44:16.650
And, oh, I mean, I love that you walk out in the morning, and there's music playing.

1110
00:44:16.890 --> 00:44:17.130
Yeah.

1111
00:44:17.650 --> 00:44:20.250
And people just might start dancing down the street.

1112
00:44:20.410 --> 00:44:20.510
Yeah.

1113
00:44:20.930 --> 00:44:22.110
I was fortunate enough.

1114
00:44:22.150 --> 00:44:24.610
I did two movies there, but I have family from Louisiana.

1115
00:44:25.030 --> 00:44:29.190
I just loved on the days that I had off, I would just go walk.

1116
00:44:30.130 --> 00:44:32.110
And you always saw something.

1117
00:44:32.350 --> 00:44:34.910
It's kind of like when you tell me stories, Jenna, about Manhattan.

1118
00:44:35.370 --> 00:44:36.710
Like, do you always see something?

1119
00:44:36.970 --> 00:44:37.110
Yeah.

1120
00:44:37.510 --> 00:44:40.130
Do you have, like, a favorite food from there?

1121
00:44:40.350 --> 00:44:42.190
Like, are you into the cuisine as well?

1122
00:44:42.510 --> 00:44:44.730
I'm not into the cuisine that much.

1123
00:44:45.030 --> 00:44:45.690
I got into the cuisine a little.

1124
00:44:45.690 --> 00:44:50.930
I don't eat shellfish or fish of any kind, so that takes a lot of it off the table.

1125
00:44:51.150 --> 00:44:54.050
But listen, just give me some red beans and rice, and I am happy.

1126
00:44:54.250 --> 00:44:54.370
Okay.

1127
00:44:54.570 --> 00:44:56.350
I do like really hot food.

1128
00:44:56.850 --> 00:45:00.930
There's really good chicken gumbo that, you know, because you don't always have to have,

1129
00:45:01.010 --> 00:45:02.450
like, the gumbo with everything in it.

1130
00:45:02.610 --> 00:45:02.770
Right.

1131
00:45:02.910 --> 00:45:05.070
There's a great gumbo at Herb Saints.

1132
00:45:05.510 --> 00:45:05.770
Okay.

1133
00:45:05.990 --> 00:45:07.810
It's my favorite restaurant in New Orleans.

1134
00:45:08.190 --> 00:45:12.170
Steve Zahn turned me on to it because he did Treme there for, like, five seasons.

1135
00:45:12.410 --> 00:45:12.590
Uh-huh.

1136
00:45:12.590 --> 00:45:16.310
I tell every single person that I know going to New Orleans to go to Herb Saints.

1137
00:45:16.730 --> 00:45:17.510
Oh, okay.

1138
00:45:17.690 --> 00:45:18.710
We're going to go next time.

1139
00:45:18.850 --> 00:45:20.030
Would that be your dream?

1140
00:45:20.030 --> 00:45:23.710
A job, like, where you live there?

1141
00:45:23.930 --> 00:45:25.770
I don't think I could live there for a long time.

1142
00:45:25.910 --> 00:45:26.250
How did you discover it?

1143
00:45:26.970 --> 00:45:28.410
My sister and I went.

1144
00:45:28.410 --> 00:45:31.570
We just needed to have a sister's weekend, and she had been there.

1145
00:45:31.630 --> 00:45:32.810
She said, oh, you're going to love it.

1146
00:45:33.170 --> 00:45:38.390
I went there with my sister, had the most amazing time, but also felt like, did I live

1147
00:45:38.390 --> 00:45:40.590
here in a past life or something?

1148
00:45:41.130 --> 00:45:43.490
Something about it felt very familiar to me.

1149
00:45:43.570 --> 00:45:43.870
Mm-hmm.

1150
00:45:44.190 --> 00:45:49.370
And I like walking down the street, and you kind of feel like you know everybody.

1151
00:45:49.990 --> 00:45:53.830
I can't explain it, but there's just so many freaks there.

1152
00:45:53.950 --> 00:45:54.070
Yeah.

1153
00:45:54.150 --> 00:45:58.570
I love people who are just, like, super friendly, and I don't know.

1154
00:45:58.670 --> 00:45:59.570
I'll take it from there.

1155
00:45:59.570 --> 00:46:00.950
I won't take it from everywhere.

1156
00:46:01.290 --> 00:46:01.430
Yeah.

1157
00:46:01.590 --> 00:46:05.790
But every time you walk down the street, to your point, there's something weird going on.

1158
00:46:05.890 --> 00:46:07.970
You're going to see something that you weren't expecting.

1159
00:46:08.410 --> 00:46:08.790
Always.

1160
00:46:08.790 --> 00:46:10.570
You know, and is it haunted?

1161
00:46:10.770 --> 00:46:12.910
Yes, but we won't get into that now.

1162
00:46:13.050 --> 00:46:13.970
That's a different podcaSt.

1163
00:46:14.390 --> 00:46:14.610
Yes.

1164
00:46:15.290 --> 00:46:18.270
But, you know, a friend of mine has this theory.

1165
00:46:18.490 --> 00:46:23.570
He's a comedy writer, and the first time he went to London, he was like, I kind of like,

1166
00:46:23.650 --> 00:46:26.610
I can't explain it exactly, but I felt it in my bones.

1167
00:46:26.810 --> 00:46:27.030
Yeah.

1168
00:46:27.270 --> 00:46:30.130
Like, I think my people were here at some time.

1169
00:46:30.270 --> 00:46:35.470
He said, I just felt so grounded in this place that I've never lived in.

1170
00:46:35.670 --> 00:46:35.830
Yeah.

1171
00:46:35.990 --> 00:46:36.770
And I don't know.

1172
00:46:36.770 --> 00:46:37.370
I feel like maybe—

1173
00:46:37.370 --> 00:46:39.250
That's how I feel about New York City.

1174
00:46:39.450 --> 00:46:39.710
Really?

1175
00:46:39.710 --> 00:46:40.790
I don't know what it is.

1176
00:46:40.890 --> 00:46:43.630
I didn't go there until I was 26 years old.

1177
00:46:43.750 --> 00:46:44.010
Uh-huh.

1178
00:46:44.090 --> 00:46:46.170
I didn't fall in love with it until my 30s.

1179
00:46:46.330 --> 00:46:51.670
But there's a piece of me that makes sense there, and it doesn't—it's never made sense

1180
00:46:51.670 --> 00:46:52.810
anywhere else in the world.

1181
00:46:52.950 --> 00:46:55.370
Have you lived there ever, or did you—you did?

1182
00:46:55.370 --> 00:46:56.450
I have a little bit.

1183
00:46:56.570 --> 00:46:56.790
Okay.

1184
00:46:56.790 --> 00:47:00.670
Yeah, but short periods of time, but I hope to retire there.

1185
00:47:00.830 --> 00:47:02.110
It's my happy place.

1186
00:47:02.250 --> 00:47:04.130
It's a magical place, too.

1187
00:47:04.310 --> 00:47:05.930
And it's the center of the universe.

1188
00:47:06.110 --> 00:47:06.930
I mean, let's be honeSt.

1189
00:47:07.090 --> 00:47:10.310
New York City, everything you need is there.

1190
00:47:10.450 --> 00:47:10.650
Yeah.

1191
00:47:11.210 --> 00:47:11.790
It's true.

1192
00:47:11.810 --> 00:47:13.350
It's such an amazing town.

1193
00:47:13.450 --> 00:47:14.170
It really is.

1194
00:47:14.630 --> 00:47:15.270
All right.

1195
00:47:15.450 --> 00:47:15.630
Okay.

1196
00:47:15.650 --> 00:47:16.590
Question number four.

1197
00:47:16.730 --> 00:47:18.350
What do you like to do on the weekends?

1198
00:47:18.930 --> 00:47:21.130
I love to putter around at home.

1199
00:47:21.130 --> 00:47:22.550
I'm not that exciting.

1200
00:47:22.770 --> 00:47:24.710
I love my animals.

1201
00:47:25.070 --> 00:47:26.990
You know, I've got seven rescue cats.

1202
00:47:27.470 --> 00:47:27.990
Seven?

1203
00:47:28.230 --> 00:47:28.430
Yeah.

1204
00:47:28.690 --> 00:47:29.430
What are their names?

1205
