Butters is the most dominant.

1206
00:47:31.810 --> 00:47:34.050
He has to be kept away from the other six.

1207
00:47:34.290 --> 00:47:36.810
He's very, very featured on your Instagram.

1208
00:47:36.970 --> 00:47:38.470
He's very—and he demands it.

1209
00:47:38.610 --> 00:47:38.830
Okay.

1210
00:47:38.910 --> 00:47:39.610
He is the hoSt.

1211
00:47:39.990 --> 00:47:40.530
What color is he?

1212
00:47:40.670 --> 00:47:42.230
He is buttery colored.

1213
00:47:42.390 --> 00:47:42.650
Okay.

1214
00:47:43.030 --> 00:47:50.170
And when you come over for skating, he will command your attention, and you will need to

1215
00:47:51.130 --> 00:47:52.870
because he expects it.

1216
00:47:52.990 --> 00:47:53.190
Okay.

1217
00:47:53.430 --> 00:47:59.690
I've got three Siamese, a mom and two of her babies, so that's Mocha, Cotton, and Gerber.

1218
00:47:59.930 --> 00:48:00.950
Are they talkative?

1219
00:48:01.450 --> 00:48:02.270
Not really.

1220
00:48:02.470 --> 00:48:02.810
Oh.

1221
00:48:02.990 --> 00:48:03.470
Not really.

1222
00:48:03.470 --> 00:48:07.490
I've always shied away from Siamese because I thought they were very vocal.

1223
00:48:07.810 --> 00:48:08.610
They are.

1224
00:48:08.790 --> 00:48:09.770
Mine are not.

1225
00:48:09.950 --> 00:48:10.170
Okay.

1226
00:48:10.370 --> 00:48:14.130
So I don't know what that's about, or maybe they only talk when I'm not there.

1227
00:48:14.290 --> 00:48:14.590
Okay.

1228
00:48:14.790 --> 00:48:23.240
My aunt had a really chatty Siamese that she named Nusance, and she'd be like,

1229
00:48:23.240 --> 00:48:24.980
Nusance, stop it.

1230
00:48:27.920 --> 00:48:30.000
That's the greatest name for a kitty.

1231
00:48:30.340 --> 00:48:30.740
I know.

1232
00:48:31.140 --> 00:48:32.420
Oh, man.

1233
00:48:32.960 --> 00:48:33.600
Nusance.

1234
00:48:33.940 --> 00:48:34.360
Nusance.

1235
00:48:35.120 --> 00:48:39.360
We have a tripod named Wabi Sabi.

1236
00:48:39.700 --> 00:48:42.780
We have a fat, fat ginger named Obi-Wan.

1237
00:48:42.900 --> 00:48:46.820
He was found strolling the streets of Hollywood as a kitten.

1238
00:48:47.100 --> 00:48:48.420
Someone gave it to me.

1239
00:48:48.420 --> 00:48:50.480
And, oh, little Jax.

1240
00:48:50.640 --> 00:48:54.200
We have a little tiger boy who was the runt of the litter.

1241
00:48:54.420 --> 00:48:54.820
Aw.

1242
00:48:55.020 --> 00:48:55.460
Jax.

1243
00:48:55.680 --> 00:48:56.820
I think that's all of them.

1244
00:48:57.020 --> 00:48:57.220
Yeah.

1245
00:48:57.720 --> 00:48:59.400
So, yeah, I love just puttering.

1246
00:48:59.600 --> 00:49:00.240
I like sewing.

1247
00:49:00.740 --> 00:49:03.080
I'm really getting into sewing more.

1248
00:49:03.340 --> 00:49:04.460
What do you sew?

1249
00:49:05.540 --> 00:49:06.040
Clothes.

1250
00:49:06.320 --> 00:49:07.120
You make clothes?

1251
00:49:07.120 --> 00:49:11.040
My dream is to sew something that I wear on the red carpet and say—

1252
00:49:11.040 --> 00:49:12.740
Oh, I want this dream to come true.

1253
00:49:12.980 --> 00:49:15.320
I want to make a show about it.

1254
00:49:16.320 --> 00:49:17.660
I hope that you will.

1255
00:49:17.820 --> 00:49:19.080
I want there to be a Rachel Ray—

1256
00:49:19.080 --> 00:49:19.660
And then you say, who are you wearing?

1257
00:49:19.740 --> 00:49:20.540
And you say, me.

1258
00:49:20.580 --> 00:49:20.920
Me.

1259
00:49:21.220 --> 00:49:22.280
I'm wearing me.

1260
00:49:22.820 --> 00:49:23.580
Thank you.

1261
00:49:23.900 --> 00:49:24.160
Okay.

1262
00:49:24.360 --> 00:49:25.540
You're going to be on this show.

1263
00:49:26.100 --> 00:49:26.920
I'm on it.

1264
00:49:27.080 --> 00:49:27.260
Yeah.

1265
00:49:27.400 --> 00:49:28.080
Bring me on.

1266
00:49:28.080 --> 00:49:32.260
I think—because getting dressed for special events is a big pain in the ass.

1267
00:49:32.300 --> 00:49:32.620
Yes.

1268
00:49:32.780 --> 00:49:32.980
Right?

1269
00:49:33.580 --> 00:49:36.520
So, why shouldn't we know how to sew our own stuff?

1270
00:49:36.520 --> 00:49:37.200
I'm sorry.

1271
00:49:37.320 --> 00:49:40.700
My mom used to sew all my formal gowns, and I always had the best gowns.

1272
00:49:40.840 --> 00:49:43.900
My mom would sew all of our, like, Easter outfits.

1273
00:49:44.720 --> 00:49:46.740
And she sewed for so long.

1274
00:49:46.920 --> 00:49:49.240
She will still—she still makes stuff all the time.

1275
00:49:49.240 --> 00:49:53.840
Like, I'm constantly bringing, like, potholders and things over to Jenna's that my mom, like,

1276
00:49:53.880 --> 00:49:55.060
was like, I had extra fabric.

1277
00:49:55.060 --> 00:49:56.040
Here's a potholder.

1278
00:49:56.140 --> 00:49:58.000
Oh, that's so sweet.

1279
00:49:58.800 --> 00:50:00.560
That's such a mom thing to do.

1280
00:50:00.760 --> 00:50:00.840
It really is.

1281
00:50:00.840 --> 00:50:01.300
That's adorable.

1282
00:50:01.380 --> 00:50:01.940
I always feel bad, though.

1283
00:50:02.220 --> 00:50:06.220
My sisters and I don't sew, and we're like, one of us needs to carry on this tradition.

1284
00:50:06.360 --> 00:50:07.900
One of us needs to learn how to do it.

1285
00:50:08.040 --> 00:50:09.360
It's so meditative.

1286
00:50:10.080 --> 00:50:10.480
Really?

1287
00:50:10.640 --> 00:50:11.840
I love cutting patterns.

1288
00:50:12.800 --> 00:50:16.720
And I've learned how to drape on a mannequin and stuff.

1289
00:50:16.740 --> 00:50:17.400
That's huge.

1290
00:50:17.720 --> 00:50:23.140
But I need to—it's like I do things in fits and starts, so I need to, like, really devote

1291
00:50:23.140 --> 00:50:23.980
some time to it.

1292
00:50:25.520 --> 00:50:30.040
But, you know, I watch a lot of TikTok, so I think, oh, now I'm a do-it-yourselfer.

1293
00:50:30.860 --> 00:50:34.780
So I make a lot of messes or I start a lot of projects that never get finished.

1294
00:50:35.800 --> 00:50:41.380
That's the show I want to watch is the DIY people that start, like, I have an Ikea hack.

1295
00:50:41.480 --> 00:50:46.020
I'm going to make a library in my foyer, and I have all this crown molding.

1296
00:50:46.100 --> 00:50:47.300
And then they're just like, f**k it.

1297
00:50:47.300 --> 00:50:48.980
And they bail halfway through.

1298
00:50:49.340 --> 00:50:50.400
That would be me.

1299
00:50:50.400 --> 00:50:52.080
That is absolutely me.

1300
00:50:52.120 --> 00:50:53.380
